iple. He worked all night. He must be exhausted."},{"type":"text","prompt":"The door is locked. They might have ___ home.","answers":["gone"],"hint":"g","explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. The door is locked. They might have gone home."},{"type":"text","prompt":"That cannot ___ Mia; she is abroad.","answers":["be"],"hint":"b","explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. That cannot be Mia; she is abroad."}]}]',total_questions=36,updated_at=1792281600000 WHERE id='B1-6.2' AND status='draft' AND total_questions=0 AND edition='' AND NOT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM navigate_assignments WHERE unit_id=navigate_units.id) AND NOT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM navigate_progress WHERE unit_id=navigate_units.id);
UPDATE navigate_units SET title='Reading the clues · Skills & review',edition='ORBIT Original Practice · 2026',status='published',steps='[{"mediaUrl":"","type":"vocabulary","skill":"vocabulary","title":"Vocabulary","instructions":"Изучи слова: послушай произношение, проверь перевод, затем выполни проверку.","words":[{"word":"exhausted","meaning":"крайне уставший"},{"word":"confused","meaning":"растерянный"},{"word":"relieved","meaning":"испытывающий облегчение"},{"word":"suspicious","meaning":"подозрительный"},{"word":"work out","meaning":"разобраться"},{"word":"rule out","meaning":"исключить вариант"},{"word":"check against","meaning":"сверить с"},{"word":"jump to conclusions","meaning":"делать поспешные выводы"}],"questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: exhausted","options":["невозможный","крайне уставший","уверенность в факте"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: exhausted — крайне уставший","word":"exhausted"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: confused","options":["растерянный","возможность","определённо"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: confused — растерянный","word":"confused"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: relieved","options":["вероятность","по-видимому","испытывающий облегчение"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: relieved — испытывающий облегчение","word":"relieved"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: suspicious","options":["должно быть","подозрительный","вывод"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: suspicious — подозрительный","word":"suspicious"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: work out","options":["разобраться","предположение","может быть"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: work out — разобраться","word":"work out"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: rule out","options":["очевидный","не может быть","исключить вариант"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: rule out — исключить вариант","word":"rule out"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: check against","options":["мог сделать в прошлом","сверить с","вероятный"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: check against — сверить с","word":"check against"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: jump to conclusions","options":["делать поспешные выводы","маловероятный","крайне уставший"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: jump to conclusions — делать поспешные выводы","word":"jump to conclusions"}]},{"mediaUrl":"/orbit-lessons/B1-6-3-4668dad52cb2.mp4","type":"video","skill":"grammar","title":"Modals of deduction","instructions":"Reading the clues / Skills & review.\nUse must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle.\n\nThe door is locked. They might have gone home.\nThat cannot be Mia; she is abroad.\nThe tea is warm. She must have left recently.","transcript":"Welcome to Orbit. Reading the clues. Our focus is Modals of deduction. Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. Listen to these examples. The door is locked. They might have gone home. That cannot be Mia; she is abroad. The tea is warm. She must have left recently. Pause the video and say one example aloud. Now practise the vocabulary and complete the tasks. You can try again and learn from every answer.","questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"Что отрабатываем в этом видео?","options":["Modals of deduction","am / is / are","there is / there are"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери предложение из объяснения.","options":["The door is locked. They might have went home.","The door is locked. They might have go home.","The door is locked. They might have gone home."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle."}],"captions":"/orbit-lessons/B1-6-3-4668dad52cb2.vtt"},{"mediaUrl":"","type":"practice","skill":"vocabulary","title":"Word builder","instructions":"Task 1 · Вспомни слово по переводу. Первая буква дана как подсказка.","questions":[{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «крайне уставший».","answers":["exhausted"],"hint":"e","explanation":"exhausted — крайне уставший."},{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «растерянный».","answers":["confused"],"hint":"c","explanation":"confused — растерянный."},{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «испытывающий облегчение».","answers":["relieved"],"hint":"r","explanation":"relieved — испытывающий облегчение."},{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «подозрительный».","answers":["suspicious"],"hint":"s","explanation":"suspicious — подозрительный."},{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «разобраться».","answers":["work out"],"hint":"w","explanation":"work out — разобраться."},{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «исключить вариант».","answers":["rule out"],"hint":"r","explanation":"rule out — исключить вариант."}]},{"mediaUrl":"","type":"practice","skill":"grammar","title":"Choose the right form","instructions":"Task 2 · Выбери подходящую форму, чтобы заполнить пропуск.","questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"The door is locked. They might have ___ home.","options":["go","gone","went"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. The door is locked. They might have gone home."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"That cannot ___ Mia; she is abroad.","options":["be","to be","being"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. That cannot be Mia; she is abroad."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"The tea is warm. She must have ___ recently.","options":["leave","leaving","left"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. The tea is warm. She must have left recently."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"She ___ be next door; I am not sure.","options":["cannot to","might","must to"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. She might be next door; I am not sure."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Her phone is on the desk. She cannot have ___ it.","options":["taken","took","take"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. Her phone is on the desk. She cannot have taken it."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"He worked all night. He must ___ exhausted.","options":["to be","being","be"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. He worked all night. He must be exhausted."}]},{"mediaUrl":"","type":"practice","skill":"grammar","title":"Put it together","instructions":"Task 3 · Нажимай на слова по порядку и собери предложение.","questions":[{"type":"order","prompt":"Собери правильное предложение.","tokens":["is","locked.","They","might","have","gone","home","The","door"],"answers":["The door is locked. They might have gone home."],"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle."},{"type":"order","prompt":"Собери правильное предложение.","tokens":["Mia;","she","is","abroad","That","cannot","be"],"answers":["That cannot be Mia; she is abroad."],"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle."},{"type":"order","prompt":"Собери правильное предложение.","tokens":["She","must","have","left","recently","The","tea","is","warm."],"answers":["The tea is warm. She must have left recently."],"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle."},{"type":"order","prompt":"Собери правильное предложение.","tokens":["I","am","not","sure","She","might","be","next","door;"],"answers":["She might be next door; I am not sure."],"explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle."}]},{"mediaUrl":"","type":"reading","skill":"reading","title":"Read the story","instructions":"The lights in the studio are off, but Mia’s bicycle is outside. She might be in the café next door. Her phone is on the desk, so she cannot have taken it with her. There is a warm cup of tea near the keyboard. She must have left only a few minutes ago, but nobody has seen her leave.","questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"What suggests she left recently?","options":["A broken chair","A warm cup of tea","An old photograph"],"answer":1,"explanation":"A warm cup of tea Ответ находится в истории этого юнита."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Has anyone seen her leave?","options":["No one has.","Everyone has.","Only the manager has."],"answer":0,"explanation":"No one has. Ответ находится в истории этого юнита."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Are the studio lights on?","options":["Yes, all of them.","Only one is on.","No, they are off."],"answer":2,"explanation":"No, they are off. Ответ находится в истории этого юнита."}]},{"mediaUrl":"/orbit-lessons/story-db84263516c0.m4a","type":"listening","skill":"listening","title":"Listen for detail","instructions":"Task 5 · Послушай историю и ответь на вопросы. Запись можно прослушать ещё раз.","transcript":"The lights in the studio are off, but Mia’s bicycle is outside. She might be in the café next door. Her phone is on the desk, so she cannot have taken it with her. There is a warm cup of tea near the keyboard. She must have left only a few minutes ago, but nobody has seen her leave.","questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"What is outside?","options":["A delivery van","Mia’s bicycle","A taxi"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Mia’s bicycle Ответ находится в истории этого юнита."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Where might Mia be?","options":["In the café next door","Definitely at the airport","Certainly abroad"],"answer":0,"explanation":"In the café next door Ответ находится в истории этого юнита."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Where is her phone?","options":["In her bag","In the café","On the desk"],"answer":2,"explanation":"On the desk Ответ находится в истории этого юнита."}]},{"mediaUrl":"","type":"practice","skill":"grammar","title":"Complete the gaps","instructions":"Task 6 · Введи пропущенное слово или выражение.","questions":[{"type":"text","prompt":"The door is locked. They might have ___ home.","answers":["gone"],"hint":"g","explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. The door is locked. They might have gone home."},{"type":"text","prompt":"That cannot ___ Mia; she is abroad.","answers":["be"],"hint":"b","explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. That cannot be Mia; she is abroad."},{"type":"text","prompt":"The tea is warm. She must have ___ recently.","answers":["left"],"hint":"l","explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. The tea is warm. She must have left recently."},{"type":"text","prompt":"She ___ be next door; I am not sure.","answers":["might"],"hint":"m","explanation":"Use must for a strong conclusion, might for a possibility, and cannot for something you believe is impossible. For past events use have plus a past participle. She might be next door; I am not sure."}]}]',total_questions=36,updated_at=1792281600000 WHERE id='B1-6.3' AND status='draft' AND total_questions=0 AND edition='' AND NOT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM navigate_assignments WHERE unit_id=navigate_units.id) AND NOT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM navigate_progress WHERE unit_id=navigate_units.id);
UPDATE navigate_units SET title='The people who matter · Words & forms',edition='ORBIT Original Practice · 2026',status='published',steps='[{"mediaUrl":"","type":"vocabulary","skill":"vocabulary","title":"Vocabulary","instructions":"Изучи слова: послушай произношение, проверь перевод, затем выполни проверку.","words":[{"word":"mentor","meaning":"наставник"},{"word":"role model","meaning":"пример для подражания"},{"word":"acquaintance","meaning":"знакомый"},{"word":"teammate","meaning":"товарищ по команде"},{"word":"relationship","meaning":"отношение между людьми"},{"word":"connection","meaning":"связь"},{"word":"generous","meaning":"щедрый"},{"word":"considerate","meaning":"внимательный к другим"}],"questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: mentor","options":["открытый новым идеям","вдохновлять","наставник"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: mentor — наставник","word":"mentor"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: role model","options":["ценить","пример для подражания","уверенный в себе"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: role model — пример для подражания","word":"role model"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: acquaintance","options":["знакомый","лёгкий в общении","уважать"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: acquaintance — знакомый","word":"acquaintance"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: teammate","options":["ладить","качество характера","товарищ по команде"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: teammate — товарищ по команде","word":"teammate"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: relationship","options":["сильная сторона","отношение между людьми","восхищаться человеком"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: relationship — отношение между людьми","word":"relationship"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: connection","options":["связь","полагаться на","слабая сторона"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: connection — связь","word":"connection"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: generous","options":["поддерживать связь","доверие","щедрый"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: generous — щедрый","word":"generous"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери перевод: considerate","options":["наставник","внимательный к другим","воодушевлять"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Выбери перевод: considerate — внимательный к другим","word":"considerate"}]},{"mediaUrl":"/orbit-lessons/B1-7-1-bf8fa089cc87.mp4","type":"video","skill":"grammar","title":"Defining and non-defining clauses","instructions":"The people who matter / Words & forms.\nUse commas for extra information in non-defining clauses. Do not use that after a comma. Use whose to show possession.\n\nMy mentor, who runs a studio, is very supportive.\nThe project that we finished won an award.\nThis is the office where we meet every Friday.","transcript":"Welcome to Orbit. The people who matter. Our focus is Defining and non-defining clauses. Use commas for extra information in non-defining clauses. Do not use that after a comma. Use whose to show possession. Listen to these examples. My mentor, who runs a studio, is very supportive. The project that we finished won an award. This is the office where we meet every Friday. Pause the video and say one example aloud. Now practise the vocabulary and complete the tasks. You can try again and learn from every answer.","questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"Что отрабатываем в этом видео?","options":["there is / there are","Defining and non-defining clauses","am / is / are"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Use commas for extra information in non-defining clauses. Do not use that after a comma. Use whose to show possession."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Выбери предложение из объяснения.","options":["My mentor, who runs a studio, is very supportive.","My mentor, that runs a studio, is very supportive.","My mentor, which runs a studio, is very supportive."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use commas for extra information in non-defining clauses. Do not use that after a comma. Use whose to show possession."}],"captions":"/orbit-lessons/B1-7-1-bf8fa089cc87.vtt"},{"mediaUrl":"","type":"practice","skill":"vocabulary","title":"Word builder","instructions":"Task 1 · Вспомни слово по переводу. Первая буква дана как подсказка.","questions":[{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «наставник».","answers":["mentor"],"hint":"m","explanation":"mentor — наставник."},{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «пример для подражания».","answers":["role model"],"hint":"r","explanation":"role model — пример для подражания."},{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «знакомый».","answers":["acquaintance"],"hint":"a","explanation":"acquaintance — знакомый."},{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «товарищ по команде».","answers":["teammate"],"hint":"t","explanation":"teammate — товарищ по команде."},{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «отношение между людьми».","answers":["relationship"],"hint":"r","explanation":"relationship — отношение между людьми."},{"type":"text","prompt":"Напиши английское слово или выражение: «связь».","answers":["connection"],"hint":"c","explanation":"connection — связь."}]},{"mediaUrl":"","type":"practice","skill":"grammar","title":"Choose the right form","instructions":"Task 2 · Выбери подходящую форму, чтобы заполнить пропуск.","questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"My mentor, ___ runs a studio, is very supportive.","options":["that","which","who"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Use commas for extra information in non-defining clauses. Do not use that after a comma. Use whose to show possession. My mentor, who runs a studio, is very supportive."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"The project ___ we finished won an award.","options":["where","that","who"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Use commas for extra information in non-defining clauses. Do not use that after a comma. Use whose to show possession. The project that we finished won an award."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"This is the office ___ we meet every Friday.","options":["where","which person","who"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use commas for extra information in non-defining clauses. Do not use that after a comma. Use whose to show possession. This is the office where we meet every Friday."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"A colleague ___ ideas I admire has joined us.","options":["who","which","whose"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Use commas for extra information in non-defining clauses. Do not use that after a comma. Use whose to show possession. A colleague whose ideas I admire has joined us."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"The studio, ___ opened last year, is growing.","options":["where","which","that"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Use commas for extra information in non-defining clauses. Do not use that after a comma. Use whose to show possession. The studio, which opened last year, is growing."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"The people ___ helped us were volunteers.","options":["who","which","where"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Use commas for extra information in non-defining clauses. Do not use that after a comma. Use whose to show possession. The people who helped us were volunteers."}]},{"mediaUrl":"","type":"practice","skill":"grammar","title":"Put it together","instructions":"Task 3 · Нажимай на слова по порядку и собери предложение.","questions":[{"type":"order","prompt":"Собери правильное предложение.","tokens":["who","runs","a","studio,","is","very","supportive","My","mentor,"],"answers":["My mentor, who runs a studio, is very supportive."],"explanation":"Use commas for extra information in non-defining clauses. Do not use that after a comma. Use whose to show possession."},{"type":"order","prompt":"Собери правильное предложение.","tokens":["we","finished","won","an","award","The","project","that"],"answers":["The project that we finished won an award."],"explanation":"Use commas for extra information in non-defining clauses.